msgid "Enable or Disable LDAP referrals.  If disabled, it may increase the speed of searches."
msgstr "Gushoboza cyangwa guhagarika iyohereza ahandi rya LDAP. Iyo rihagaritswe, bishobora kongera umuvuduko w'ishakisha."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Uburyo"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Mode which cacti will attempt to authenticate against the LDAP server.<blockquote><i>No Searching</i> - No Distinguished Name (DN) searching occurs, just attempt to bind with the provided Distinguished Name (DN) format.<br><br><i>Anonymous Searching</i> - Attempts to search for username against LDAP directory via anonymous binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>Specific Searching</i> - Attempts search for username against LDAP directory via Specific Distinguished Name (DN) and Specific Password for binding to locate the users Distinguished Name (DN).<br><br><i>One-Time Passwords (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti binds the user password only once, during final authentication.  <i>No Searching</i> performs no directory lookup and binds directly using the Distinguished Name (DN) template, so it is safe for OTP when the DN template alone identifies the user.  When a directory lookup is required to resolve the DN, use <i>Specific Searching</i> with a dedicated service account (or <i>Anonymous Searching</i> where the directory permits it) so the lookup never consumes the single-use code.  For resilient OTP deployments use a single DNS load balancer name in the Server(s) field rather than a space delimited multi-server list, which would re-attempt the bind with an already-consumed one-time password."
msgstr "Uburyo cacti izagerageza kwemeza umwirondoro kuri seriveri ya LDAP.<blockquote><i>Nta gushakisha</i> - Nta gushakisha Izina Ryihariye (DN) bibaho, gerageza gusa guhuza ukoresheje imiterere y'Izina Ryihariye (DN) yatanzwe.<br><br><i>Gushakisha utazwi</i> - Igerageza gushakisha izina ry'ukoresha mu bubiko bwa LDAP binyuze mu guhuza utazwi kugira ngo ibone Izina Ryihariye (DN) ry'ukoresha.<br><br><i>Gushakisha kwihariye</i> - Igerageza gushakisha izina ry'ukoresha mu bubiko bwa LDAP binyuze mu Izina Ryihariye (DN) ryihariye n'Ijambo ry'ibanga ryihariye mu guhuza kugira ngo ibone Izina Ryihariye (DN) ry'ukoresha.<br><br><i>Amagambo y'ibanga akoreshwa rimwe (OTP/MFA)</i> - Cacti ihuza ijambo ry'ibanga ry'ukoresha inshuro imwe gusa, mu gihe cyo kwemeza umwirondoro kwa nyuma.  <i>Nta gushakisha</i> ntikora ishakisha mu bubiko kandi ihuza ako kanya ikoresheje urugero rw'Izina Ryihariye (DN), bityo birizewe kuri OTP iyo urugero rwa DN rwonyine rugaragaza ukoresha.  Iyo hakenewe gushakisha mu bubiko kugira ngo haboneke DN, koresha <i>Gushakisha kwihariye</i> hamwe na konti ya serivisi yabugenewe (cyangwa <i>Gushakisha utazwi</i> aho ububiko bubyemera) kugira ngo ishakisha ritigera rikoresha kode ikoreshwa rimwe.  Ku mikoreshereze ya OTP yizewe, koresha izina rimwe rya DNS rigabanya umutwaro mu mwanya wa Server(s) aho gukoresha urutonde rwa seriveri nyinshi zitandukanijwe n'umwanya, ibyo bikaba byakongera kugerageza guhuza n'ijambo ry'ibanga rikoreshwa rimwe ryamaze gukoreshwa."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "Distinguished Name (DN)"
msgstr "Izina Rihariwe (DN)"

#: login_providers.php
msgid "The \"Distinguished Name\" syntax, applicable for both OpenLDAP and Windows AD configurations, offers flexibility in defining user identity. For OpenLDAP, the format follows this structure: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD provides an alternative syntax: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, commonly known as \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". In this context, \"&lt;username&gt;\" represents the specific username provided during the login prompt. This is particularly pertinent when operating in \"No Searching\" mode, or \"Require Group Membership\" enabled."
msgstr "Imyandikire ya \"Izina Rihariwe (DN)\", ikoreshwa ku igenamiterere rya OpenLDAP na Windows AD, itanga uburyo bworoshye bwo gusobanura umwirondoro w'umukoresha. Kuri OpenLDAP, imiterere ikurikiza iyi nyubako: <i>\"uid=&lt;username&gt;,ou=people,dc=domain,dc=local\"</i>. Windows AD itanga indi myandikire: <i>\"&lt;username&gt;@win2kdomain.local\"</i>, izwi cyane nka \"userPrincipalName (UPN)\". Muri ubu buryo, \"&lt;username&gt;\" ihagarariye izina ry'umukoresha ryihariye ryatanzwe mu gihe cyo kwinjira. Ibi ni ingenzi cyane igihe hakoreshwa uburyo bwa \"Nta Shakisha\", cyangwa iyo \"Gusaba Kuba mu Itsinda\" bishobojwe."

#: login_providers.php
msgid "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "uid=<username>,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com"

